ill. W-W-Whatcha doin'?” “Eh, nothing adventurous. You know that race of Underground Dwelling Cannibal Horse People that we're always fighting?” “Yeah, the CHUDs. W-W-What about 'em? “Well, don't tell anybody, but I'm working on a bioweapon to use against them, so I got this barrel of horse semen from your mom's hospital and I'm just gonna, you know, subject it to some otherworldly forces.”","ref":"2021 July 11, Nick Rutherford, “Rickdependence Spray” (1:10 from the start), in Rick and Morty, season 5, episode 4, spoken by Rick Sanchez (Justin Roiland):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,28]],"id":"7df8c7a1-e490-447c-9c71-6edea99c751f"}],"categories":["American English","Australian English","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","New Zealand English","Philippine English"],"links":[["friend","friend"],["address","address"]],"raw_glosses":["(US, Australia, New Zealand, Philippines) A close friend; especially used as a form of address."],"glosses":["A close friend; especially used as a form of address."],"tags":["Australia","New-Zealand","Philippines","US","colloquial","endearing"],"id":"be9ea563-1149-4138-87d4-bbf40c4beabd"},{"examples":[{"text":"The books say it's normal. Toddlers often stop napping around this age, and the average amount of sleep needed by a two-year-old is between nine and thirteen hours. My kiddo cuts logs for twelve hours at a stretch, so she's plenty rested.","ref":"2008, Robin Dutton-Cookston, The Foggiest Idea: Tales of a Displaced Texan in San Francisco Mamaland, page 51:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[168,173]],"id":"4546db4b-1aa6-456d-937f-5498a5f6d195"}],"categories":["American English","Australian English","English terms with quotations","New Zealand English","Philippine English","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["child","child"]],"raw_glosses":["(US, Australia, New Zealand, Philippines) A child."],"glosses":["A child."],"tags":["Australia","New-Zealand","Philippines","US","co